\meta{commit}{45563d9}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Two corner cases of the arena, \code{\verb~|eta-struct-major-no-whnf~} and \code{\verb~|eta-struct-major-and-no-whnf~}, make the official kernel loop: it does not terminate, and the arena records a timeout. The reference kernel had the same loop and ran into the 60 s timeout without allocating. Its delta loops (weak head normal form, lazy delta reduction, lazy delta under projections) now detect a return to a state they were in before and decline the judgment, saying that the reduction returns to a term it started from. Both tests decline in 0.2 s. 110 unit tests are green and all 230 published tests stay correct.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-ref/README.md}. Commit \commit{45563d9}. Session: [foundation modules and the reference pipeline](ses-BQZM). Related: [the two tests on which the official checker does not terminate](ex-9ECC).}
